+            <h2>How a cup works</h2>
+            <ol class="about-steps">
+                <li>
+                    <h3>Edits enter</h3>
+                    <p>A set of fan edits is chosen for the cup. You can see all of them in the <a href="/music-gallery">gallery</a>.</p>
+                </li>
+                <li>
+                    <h3>The draw</h3>
+                    <p>Edits are ranked by views and likes into four pots, and each group of four gets one edit from every pot. The strongest edits can't knock each other out in the groups.</p>
+                </li>
+                <li>
+                    <h3>You vote</h3>
+                    <p>Each match is two edits side by side. Watch both and vote for the one you like more. You get one vote per match, and the live split appears once you have voted.</p>
+                </li>
+                <li>
+                    <h3>Top two go through</h3>
+                    <p>In each group, the two edits with the most wins advance. If wins are level, the share of the votes decides.</p>
+                </li>
+                <li>
+                    <h3>Knockout to champion</h3>
+                    <p>From there it's single elimination: win and you go on, lose and your run ends. The last edit standing is the champion.</p>
+                </li>
+            </ol>
+        </section>
+
+        <section class="about-card" id="fair">
+            <h2>Fair play</h2>
